@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] ios-host-renders-shared-compose
The iOS host MUST render the shared Pully Compose controller. It MUST NOT duplicate
Pully screens or business rules in Swift. Native code MAY adapt system lifecycle,
authentication, storage, links, input, navigation and device services. Source: Tavi,
21 Oct 2026, chosen Compose Multiplatform implementation with maximum Android reuse.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ios-preview-is-explicit
Until server/account and review flows are connected, the iOS app MUST identify itself
as an internal preview and MUST use deterministic nonprivate fixtures. Unsupported
sign-in, mutation and AI controls MUST NOT appear as working features. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 iOS implementation request and the accepted first shared-screen milestone.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] ios-bundled-locales-match-web
The iOS app bundle's `i18n/` JSON locale set and each file's bytes MUST equal
`packages/app/src/i18n/locales`. The host MUST package the existing Android mirror
without maintaining another set of translation files. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
maximum-reuse iOS decision and DESIGN.md's locale source-of-truth enforcement.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] ios-feedback-is-native-output-of-shared-cuelume
iOS control feedback MUST synthesize the existing shared Cuelume recipes and DSP.
Native code MAY adapt PCM output and system haptic generators, but MUST NOT replace
the cue signatures with generic system sounds. It MUST respect the saved sound and
haptic preferences, Ring/Silent, and suspension; suspended feedback MUST NOT replay
on resume. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision and Android
sound-follows-the-phone, sound-cue-per-role and DESIGN.md rule 125.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-keychain-tests-use-real-private-app-identity
The iOS Keychain roundtrip MUST execute the actual secure-store adapter in a
genuine app-hosted simulator test with its own private application identifier in
the code-signed executable. The harness MUST verify the built signature and the
actual matching XML/DER simulator entitlements embedded in that executable,
MUST NOT widen Keychain sharing, and MUST NOT skip or mock a missing entitlement
as a passing result. Source: Tavi's chosen 21 Oct 2026 native-storage plan and
the real simulator errSecMissingEntitlement failure; Apple DTS app-host guidance
and Xcode's simulator entitlement representation observed in the 21 Oct Mac run.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] ios-home-services-follow-actual-scene-lifecycle
Shared Home actions MUST use native clipboard writes and external HTTPS GitHub
navigation, bypassing the app's incoming-link router. Lifecycle registration MUST
synchronously report the current scene state, then real scene transitions;
cancellation MUST remove exactly that registration, and disconnection MUST stop
and release all observers. An obsolete reentrant foreground event MUST NOT resume
background work. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse plan and shared Home
NativeHomeActions contract, preserving Android foreground lifecycle ownership.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;motion] ios-edge-back-drives-shared-navigation
The iOS leading-edge recognizer MUST report normalized progress and commit or cancel
to the existing shared PageMotion and navigation stack. It MUST use the shared
layout direction, reject disabled root navigation, cancel on scene interruption,
and release replaced or cancelled registrations. It MUST NOT transform the native
controller or maintain another route stack. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse
iOS plan and the shared NativeHomeActions edge-back integration decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] ios-explicit-browser-uses-native-web-presentation
The shared explicit browser action MUST accept only HTTP(S) URLs with a host and no
URL credentials, and MUST present the native browser controller from the active
scene. Its initial navigation MUST bypass Pully and GitHub universal-link routing.
The separate open-on-GitHub action MAY use direct system navigation. Neither action
MAY forward Pully RPC or Access credentials. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse
iOS plan and the shared Overview browser action through NativeHomeActions.
